   "caption": "Leaf disc infection assay in the presence of Pseudomonas donghuensis R32 and Pseudomonas chlororaphis R47. Leaf discs from the Bintje cultivar were infected with Phytophthora infestans GFP zoospores and, at the same time, inoculated with different genotypes of R32 and R47. Each treatment was tested on 20 individual leaf discs. (A) Lesion formation was scored from 1 (no lesion) to 5 (full necrosis) at 4 dpi. Statistical analysis was performed with a Kruskal–Wallis test followed by Dunn's test. (B) Mycelium formation was scored from 1 (no mycelium) to 5 (extensive mycelium) at 5 dpi. The same statistical analysis as for the lesion score was performed. (C) Pictures from one representative leaf disc per treatment are shown. GFP, green fluorescent protein; WT, wild type.",
